 R←Test_UC_029(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;rc;msg;result;stop;status
⍝ Runs ]Add with a file name that contains a slash, together with -project=. The dispatcher had a
⍝ special case that took any argument containing a slash for the project folder - right for
⍝ ]AddGitIgnore, wrong for ]Add, whose argument is a file. It also bypassed <GetSpaceAndFolder>,
⍝ the only place where -project= is read, so that switch was silently ignored.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed
 stop←0

 tempDir←FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir'APLGit2-',⊃⎕SI
 (##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/CiderProject4.zip')ZipArchive.UnzipTo tempDir
 (⊂' r←Counter' ' r←4711')⎕NPUT(tempDir,'/APLSource/Counter.aplf')1

 (rc msg result)←stop ∆UCMD'Add APLSource/Counter.aplf -project="',tempDir,'"'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠rc

 status←0 1 G.Status tempDir
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≠≢status
 →T.GoToTidyUp'M'≠⊃status[1;1]                    ⍝ Staged, so the index column says "M"
 →T.GoToTidyUp'APLSource/Counter.aplf'≢⊃status[1;3]

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
